        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "2 months ago",
        "text": "Very reactive and understanding. I appreciate the help I received from this office.",
        "time": 1764126545,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Murray Levine",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116080014744202337358/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXe2JLhfjVNPJPBwMl3ABdJ2shJD85xJXGvjEIOnMnmscfOhHrdrQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 3,
        "relative_time_description": "12 months ago",
        "text": "Peter has the nicest smile in the House of Commons!\nHe is a hundred times better than my previous MP Anju Dhillon BUT if there was ever a totally useless MP, it’s Anju!\nWhat’s 100X0?\nI moved from Dorval almost 3 years ago to Vaudreuil due to a life threatening pollutant emanating from aircraft at YUL.\nI had great expectations of Peter due to his history concerning the environment.\nWhat a terrible disappointment he has been for around 18 months.\nWhat does YUL have to do with this riding. Actually very little BUT he is my MP and when I moved to Vaudreuil Anju Dhillon was no longer obliged essentially to listen to me!\nDon’t ever expect any politician to solve any problem. Solving problems requires intelligence.\nAs long as candidates in elections are not offered optional psychometric testing, and the results are not published, we will end up with what we deserve, for not demanding it!",
        "time": 1739980212,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Sam Vekemans",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117921658240148036148/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWTA39k0vJEkXAtoHTV27MkH4rVrUtnlzF8HF_zpY45c_kxbR1LOw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "9 years ago",
        "text": "\"PS: We can't afford not to change our policy on marijuana. It hasn't worked. Every single government that has tried to fight the marijuana problem by throwing money at it has lost all its money. We saw it under (U.S. President) Ronald Reagan 'Say No to Drugs.' Tens of billions of dollars were invested and the rate of use of marijuana barely budged. Part of the population will smoke marijuana whether it's legal or not. Our plan is to look at what's happening around the world. There are countries who have decriminalized marijuana and have done it successfully. The result is the money has been taken out of the pockets of the crime syndicates. \" yourlocaljournal dot ca",
        "time": 1461407753,
        "translated": false
      },
